A||||2||FieroGT||Bad things happened to my GT.....||||9||
Z||000000||FieroGT||03-17-2000||02:10 PM||||Last Saturday, I took the GT out for the evening; I usually drive it on the nice weekends. Well, I went over to a friend's house for a get-together, and found out that there was no place to park. His parents live 3 houses up the alley, so I parked my car perpendicular to their garage door, since it was late and figured that they weren't going anywhere. I was at my bud's house for about 30 minutes when his phone rang. It was his Mom, asking if it was my car parked outside the garage. I got on the phone and she said that she opened the garage door to leave and just backed out. Unfortunately, my GT was sitting in the path of the Grand Cherokee. I ran up to discover that she nailed it right behind the RR wheel. Fortunately for me, all that was damaged was the marker light, which snapped in half. Moral of the story......don't be dumb like me and park your car where others can't see it. <P>If anyone has a smooth-moulding right rear side marker light for sale, give me a holler because I need one. Thanks.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Old Lar||03-17-2000||03:13 PM||||Check with Mr Goodwrench.  I just found in stock the front side markers for the GT. I bought two for each side for a rainy day. They may have the rear moldings in stock.  Rather pricy plastic at $30 plus a pop.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||03-18-2000||11:30 PM||||Check the Fiero Store . I got one there for mine after my wife backed my coupe into the garage...lol...OH WELL.||||reg||6
